Safety scope: the private quantization/framing module forbids unsafe code and
base64 0.22 also forbids it. This is NOT a zero-unsafe transitive claim. Existing
image buffer views, PNG/zlib/checksum implementations and terminal OS bindings
still use internal unsafe code. The consuming application must validate bounded
worker RGBA, never decode source image formats here, cap its render/cache sizes,
and retain those narrowly reviewed renderer/system-service exceptions. Keep
chafa-dyn/chafa-static and image-defaults disabled for Nuschl.

Vendoring omits upstream Cargo.lock, registry bookkeeping and showcase.gif. The
library source, public API, examples, benchmark, build script and original
manifest are otherwise retained; Cargo.toml and Cargo.toml.orig reflect this
small dependency substitution. Tests use generated fixtures; upstream tests
expecting unpublished assets are outside the focused vendor-safety filter.
